IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gst-types`

-- Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 — GOALS 4 AND 5: ASSESSMENT, REVIEW AND
-- APPEAL; COLLECTION, REFUNDS AND RULINGS.
--
--   Goal 4: "May the Comptroller still assess this period; how long must
--            records be kept; when are objections and appeals due, and may
--            the appeal be heard?"
--   Goal 5: "How is tax collected and refunded — agents, security, travel
--            bans, refund claims, rulings — and when is a notice served?"
--
-- Source: ../source/GSTA1993.txt — Parts 7, 8, 10-12 and the Fifth Schedule.

§ `Goal 4 — assessment, records, review and appeal`

-- s 45(5): no assessment "(a) ... for a prescribed accounting period ending
-- before 1 January 2007, more than 7 years after the end of the prescribed
-- accounting period; and (b) ... ending on or after 1 January 2007, more than
-- 5 years after". (5A): fraud or wilful default — "at any time".
@ref s 45(5)-(5A), (8)
GIVEN `period ended` IS A DATE, `fraud or wilful default` IS A BOOLEAN, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Comptroller may still assess, period ended` `period ended` `, fraud:` `fraud or wilful default` `, as at` `as at` IF
    `fraud or wilful default` OR `as at` AT MOST `the last day for an assessment` `period ended`

GIVEN `period ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for an assessment` `period ended` MEANS
    IF `period ended` LESS THAN YMD 2007 1 1
    THEN `add years` `period ended` 7
    ELSE `add years` `period ended` 5

-- s 46(2): records kept "(a) ... not less than 7 years" for periods ending
-- before 2007, "(b) ... not less than 5 years" after. s 47(2A): an
-- anti-avoidance adjustment "must not be made more than 5 years after the end
-- of the prescribed accounting period". s 45(10B): a return made more than
-- 5 years after its period is treated as not made.
@ref ss 46(2), 47(2A), 45(10B)
GIVEN `period ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`records must be kept until, period ended` `period ended` MEANS `the last day for an assessment` `period ended`

-- s 47(4): the anti-avoidance rule "does not apply to any arrangement carried
-- out for bona fide commercial reasons and had not as one of its main purposes
-- the avoidance or reduction of tax". s 47A(2): a surcharge of 50% of the
-- additional tax for periods from 1 January 2021.
@ref s 47(1), (4)
GIVEN `a purpose or effect of a tax advantage` IS A BOOLEAN, `bona fide commercial, without a main tax purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Comptroller must counteract the arrangement, tax advantage:` `a purpose or effect of a tax advantage` `, bona fide:` `bona fide commercial, without a main tax purpose` IF
    `a purpose or effect of a tax advantage` AND (NOT `bona fide commercial, without a main tax purpose`)

@ref s 47A(1)-(2)
GIVEN `additional tax` IS A NUMBER, `period starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 47A surcharge on additional tax` `additional tax` `, period starting` `period starts` MEANS
    IF `period starts` AT LEAST YMD 2021 1 1 THEN `additional tax` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100 ELSE 0

-- ss 45A(3), 47(2C), 47A(3), 89(2B): payable "within one month after the date
-- a written notice ... is served".
@ref ss 45A(3), 47(2C), 47A(3), 89(2B)
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a surcharge or additional tax is due by, notice served` served MEANS `add months` served 1

-- s 48(1): penal tax "not exceeding 3 times the amount of tax which has or
-- would have been undercharged".
@ref s 48(1)
GIVEN undercharged IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penal tax on undercharged tax of` undercharged MEANS undercharged TIMES 3

-- s 49(2): an objection "within 30 days after the date the person has been
-- notified of the decision". s 51(1): a notice of appeal "within 30 days after
-- the date of the decision of the Comptroller on the application for review",
-- and a petition "within 30 days after the date on which such notice of appeal
-- was lodged"; (3) else the notice is withdrawn.
@ref s 49(2)
GIVEN notified IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object, notified` notified MEANS notified PLUS 30

@ref s 51(1)(a)
GIVEN decided IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give notice of appeal, review decided` decided MEANS decided PLUS 30

@ref s 51(1)(b), (3)
GIVEN `notice lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to lodge the petition of appeal, notice lodged` `notice lodged` MEANS `notice lodged` PLUS 30

-- s 51(7): no hearing unless all returns are made and the amounts shown paid.
-- (8): for an appeal on the tax chargeable, an assessment or security, the
-- tax must be "paid or deposited" unless, for hardship, the Comptroller agrees
-- or the Board decides.
@ref s 51(7)-(8)
GIVEN `returns made and paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `about tax, an assessment or security` IS A BOOLEAN, `tax paid or deposited` IS A BOOLEAN, `hardship allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may hear the appeal, returns:` `returns made and paid` `, tax matter:` `about tax, an assessment or security` `, paid:` `tax paid or deposited` `, hardship:` `hardship allowed` IF
        `returns made and paid`
    AND ((NOT `about tax, an assessment or security`) OR `tax paid or deposited` OR `hardship allowed`)

-- s 52(1)(b): notice of the hearing "not later than 14 days before the
-- hearing".
@ref s 52(1)(b)
GIVEN hearing IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`notice of the Board hearing is due by, hearing` hearing MEANS hearing MINUS 14

-- s 54(2): appeal to the High Court on law or mixed law and fact "except on
-- any case where the Board has determined that the tax payable or any amount
-- due to the appellant is less than $500 excluding the amount of costs".
@ref s 54(2)
GIVEN `amount determined` IS A NUMBER, `on law or mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may appeal to the High Court, amount` `amount determined` `, on law:` `on law or mixed law and fact` IF
    `on law or mixed law and fact` AND `amount determined` AT LEAST 500

-- s 50(6): a committee of "not less than 3 members", including the Chairperson
-- or a Deputy; (6A) or a single member who is Chairperson or Deputy.
@ref s 50(6)-(6A)
GIVEN members IS A NUMBER, `includes the Chairperson or a Deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is properly constituted, members` members `, chair or deputy:` `includes the Chairperson or a Deputy` IF
    `includes the Chairperson or a Deputy` AND (members AT LEAST 3 OR members EQUALS 1)

§ `Goal 5 — collection, refunds, rulings and service`

-- s 90(1B)(b): a refund claim "within 5 years after" the end of the period
-- (or the date of payment). s 90(1A): for periods ending on or after 1 January
-- 2007.
@ref s 90(1A)-(1B)
GIVEN `period ended or tax paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to claim a refund, from` `period ended or tax paid` MEANS
    IF `period ended or tax paid` LESS THAN YMD 2007 1 1
    THEN REFUSE "s 90(1A) covers only periods ending, and supplies made, on or after 1 January 2007; s 90(5) allows no other refund"
    ELSE `add years` `period ended or tax paid` 5

-- s 79(2): a declared agent pays from moneys held "at the date of receipt of
-- the notice or at any time not later than 90 days thereafter". (4)(a): for a
-- joint account, notify the owners "within 14 days" and pay "within 42 days";
-- (c) an owner objects "within 28 days"; (d)(ii) the agent tells the
-- Comptroller "within 7 days". (4)(b): joint holders are presumed to own
-- equal shares.
@ref s 79(2)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`moneys held until this day are caught by the agency notice, received` received MEANS received PLUS 90

@ref s 79(4)(a)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`an agent must pay over from a joint account by, notice received` received MEANS received PLUS 42

@ref s 79(4)(b)
GIVEN balance IS A NUMBER, holders IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the presumed share of one joint holder, balance` balance `, holders` holders MEANS balance DIVIDED BY holders

-- s 60(2) is in Goal 6. s 83J(2): an owner told to collect items within "at
-- least 5 days". s 83E(7): an arrested person held at most "48 hours,
-- excluding the time necessary for the journey".
@ref s 83E(7)
GIVEN `hours held, excluding the journey` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detention is within time, hours` `hours held, excluding the journey` IF
    `hours held, excluding the journey` AT MOST 48

-- Fifth Schedule Part 2 para 1: an advance ruling costs "$660 (inclusive of
-- tax)", plus "$165 ... per hour (or any part of an hour), beyond the first
-- 4 hours"; an expedited ruling up to "2 times the aggregate". Part 1 para 6:
-- a ruling applies "for a period of 3 years beginning on the date the ruling is
-- made": the last day is the day before the third anniversary.
@ref Fifth Schedule Part 2 para 1(1)(a)-(c)
GIVEN `hours spent` IS A NUMBER, expedited IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most an advance ruling costs, hours` `hours spent` `, expedited:` expedited MEANS
    IF expedited THEN `base` TIMES 3 ELSE `base`
    WHERE
        `base` MEANS 660 PLUS 165 TIMES `chargeable hours`
        `chargeable hours` MEANS
            IF `hours spent` AT MOST 4 THEN 0
            ELSE IF FLOOR (`hours spent` MINUS 4) EQUALS (`hours spent` MINUS 4)
                 THEN `hours spent` MINUS 4
                 ELSE FLOOR (`hours spent` MINUS 4) PLUS 1

@ref Fifth Schedule Part 1 para 6(b)
GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`an advance ruling applies until, made` made MEANS (`add years` made 3) MINUS 1

-- s 87(3A): a notice through the electronic service is served "when an
-- electronic record of it enters the person's account"; (2) by post, when it
-- "would have been received in the ordinary course of post" (an input).
@ref s 87(2), (3A)
GIVEN m IS A `Service mode`, sent IS A DATE, `ordinary course of post` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the notice is served on, mode` m `, sent` sent `, post would arrive` `ordinary course of post` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `ordinary or registered post` THEN `ordinary course of post`
    OTHERWISE sent

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 41(1)-(6), (8), 42-44, 45(1)-(4), (6)-(11), 46(1)-(1D), (3)-(5), 47(1A)-(3), 48(2)-(5), 49(1), (3), 50, 51(2), (5)-(6), (9)-(11), 52-57, 68-74, 76-78, 79(1), (3), (5)-(6), 80-85, 86-88, 89, 90(1AA)-(1AD), (1C)-(5), 90A, 92-94; Fifth, Sixth, Tenth Schedules
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`administration provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 41-44: returns, invoices, price display, the electronic service, receipts"
         "ss 45-48: best-judgment assessments, assessments of goods unaccounted for, supplementary assessments, the records to keep, anti-avoidance adjustments, penal tax"
         "Part 8: the matters reviewable, the Board's constitution, hearings, onus (and s 52(3A)), powers, costs, cases stated, privacy, finality"
         "Part 10: prosecution, Public Prosecutor's consent for ss 6, 62, 62C, 63, 65, 66, evidence, certificates, summons, notices to attend court, liability of officers and principals, jurisdiction, Customs Act procedure"
         "Part 11: recovery as a debt and from invoices showing tax, agents, indemnity, security, travel bans, samples, seizure, forfeiture, arrest, examination, access and information powers, informers"
         "Part 12: authorised officers, orders and regulations, service, free postage, remission, refunds of overpaid tax and unjust enrichment, advance rulings, the 2020-2024 transitional rules"
         "Fifth, Sixth and Tenth Schedules: ruling procedure, public schemes and published lists, prescribed information"
